From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niko Lowry <niko@neeks.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:28:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] llm: size the predicted KV cache per layer

PredictServerVRAM sized every layer's KV cache with the smallest
head_count_kv, embedding_length/head_count as the head size, the full
context, and f16. For models that differ per layer that is far off.
gemma4:31b at 262144 context with OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 was
predicted at 57.9 GiB; llama-server allocated 31.0 GiB. The scheduler
evicted models to make room the load never needed, and the inflated
prediction also triggered metal_partial_offload, which turns off mmap.

The estimate now follows llama.cpp's allocation: per-layer
head_count_kv, key_length and value_length (with the _swa variants),
and the configured cache type. Sliding-window layers hold the window
plus one batch per sequence, sized with max(2048, num_batch), since an
explicit num_batch reaches llama-server as -ub. Non-causal models keep
no cache. Unquantized caches size V at the widest layer, as llama.cpp
does without flash attention.

Layers llama.cpp gives no cache of their own are skipped: layers with
no KV heads; recurrent layers of qwen3next, qwen35 and qwen35moe;
the gemma layers that read an earlier layer's cache; and MTP layers
unless draft_num_predict is set. A deepseek2 MLA cache stores K only.
PredictServerVRAM takes the request's options for num_batch and
draft_num_predict.

Measured against llama-server, q8_0 cache:

  gemma4:31b        262144   57.9 -> 30.4 GiB   measured 31.0
  qwen3-coder-next  262144   54.2 -> 51.4 GiB   measured 52.4
  qwen3.5:0.8b       32768   KV 816 -> 204 MiB  allocated 204.00
  gemma4:e2b         32768   KV 275 -> 118 MiB  allocated 111.56

The compute graph and the recurrent state of hybrid models are still
not counted; the scheduler's 20% headroom covers them.

